@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/simulation#> .
@prefix intention: <http://example.org/orexis/intention#> .
@prefix desire: <http://example.org/orexis/desire#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix ssn: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix review: <http://example.org/orexis/review#> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix water: <http://example.org/orexis/water#> .
@prefix reporting: <http://example.org/orexis/reporting#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix market: <http://example.org/orexis/market#> .

#  Fern's agent's PRIVATE beliefs — the parameters for the capabilities it composed.
#
#  Grouped by the module that reads them. A module never reads outside its own vocabulary,
#  so adding a capability means adding a block here, and nothing else changes.
#
#  Nothing here is repeated from the world: the wiring (which plant, which sensor, which
#  market) is stated once, publicly, there. This file is only what fern *thinks*.

##  sensing:Subscribing — the interval it asks its board to keep
:fern_agent
    sensing:fastSleepS 30 ;          # at/below its own low band: watch closely
    sensing:slowSleepS 600 ;         # comfortable: let the board sleep, save energy
    sensing:readingGraceS 45 ;     # slack past the cadence it asked for, before it calls the sensor quiet
    sensing:alarmDeltaFraction 0.25 .  # what counts as a jolt: this fraction of a band's width,
                                       # moved since the board's last report. A first pick, not a
                                       # bound — the world grants room on it, and review re-picks

##  market:Bidding — what it aims at and what it will pay
#
#  The bands that used to sit here are gone. Where a fern is parched and where it is soaked are
#  facts about the FERN, stated in world.ttl as an operating range and a survival range, and
#  `desire:Deducing` intersects them into the region this agent holds. Restating them privately
#  meant keeping a second copy of a public fact and being free to keep a wrong one.
#
#  The target is gone too — it became the AIM, under desire at the end of this file, because
#  the point an agent steers for is a fact about its ends and not about a market. What is left
#  here is what only a BID needs: the wallet and the value curve.
:fern_agent
    market:hasEndowment 100.0 ;
    water:litresPerFraction 2.0 ;  # what it BELIEVES its pot takes (the world knows the truth)
    market:tolerance 0.5 ;         # how close a lot must land to what that conversion predicts (#518)
    water:maxValuePerL 0.80 .      # willingness to pay at peak urgency — never disclosed

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
#   Omit this line and the agent reports nothing; see orexis/metrics.py.
:fern_agent reporting:metricsIntervalS 60 .

##  Self-review — how often at the very least.
#   Required because the world gave this agent room to move (review:commits, in world.ttl): an
#   agent granted none derives no review capability and needs no interval. A FLOOR and not a
#   schedule — a decision plans its own next arising from when its effect could show.
#   See knowledge/decisions/self-review-is-a-capability.md.
:fern_agent review:reviewIntervalS 300 .

##  desire — the pick inside the region
#   The point this agent steers its moisture toward. PRIVATE where the region is public: the
#   region is deduced from what the plant states and answers to the sovereign; the aim answers
#   to the region (sensing:AimShape) and to nobody else, which is what makes it this agent's.
#   It used to be water:hasTarget — one number that was also the market's pricing input. The
#   market now asks desire for it, so an agent in a world with no market could still hold one.
:fern_agent sensing:aims [ ssn:forProperty water:SoilMoisture ; schema:value 0.55 ] .

##  intention — the commitment policy
#   How long a standing commitment absorbs a second impulse to do the same thing before a new
#   adoption may supersede it. The ledger records what this agent does either way; the patience
#   is what makes "already doing something about it" a fact with teeth. Two minutes: several
#   auction rounds, and far past any one bid window.
:fern_agent orexis:patienceS 120 .
